#
# WHY A FILE AND NOT THE GIT INDEX (jacob-greene/nexus#182, skeptic finding 1):
# reading the index reports a count, it does not pin one. `git rm <fixture>`
# drops the name from the index AND the working tree, so an index-derived
# count falls from 30 to 29 and agrees with itself. The suite then ran one
# assertion fewer at exit 0 under ALL TESTS PASSED — the very defect this
# file exists to close. A tracked manifest cannot be defeated that way:
# removing a fixture without editing this file fails the suite, and editing
# this file is a reviewable diff.
#
# It also needs no git, so the suite is fully accounted for in an export,
# a tarball, or any tree with no index.
#
# One basename per line. Blank lines and # comments are ignored. A repeated
# name is an error: the suite fails and names it.
